7|0@Denver^1440550558#cufqsby:Kilomyles$:Sorry to hear that :( This will be my 2nd assault in the 6 years I've lived down here. Hey I can tell you guys this story! So I use to work at the office depot at Colfax and would open the store at 6 in the morning with my manager. I lived 1.5 blocks away, I would roll out of bed and walk to work 10 minutes before my shift. This particular morning I was wearing my headphones and drinking a cup of chai, approaching the cross walk. On the other side a woman and her kid were walking towards me, and she motions for me to take my earbuds out. It's important to note she had luggage, and in hindsight she was probably homeless or recently so. She asks me for a cigarette. "Sorry, I don't smoke cigarettes and I'm on my way to work" I say this because I dont smoke cigs, but I smoke pot, and it use to be my tounge in cheek way of saying I like to smoke pot. I was also walking fast, so hence saying im on my way to work. As I pass them, I see a guy behind them I didn't notice before. He asks me the same thing, to which I say: "I don't smoke cigs." Shorter, more brief since I thought he may of heard me, and again in hindsight he was probably the father/husband. Well I pass him and he starts to follow me. "Hold up!" he says. "I can't I got to get to work." I say over my shoulder. Anna hated when I was late. "No, you need to wait, you were being disrespectful." Here's a critical moment. I turn half around and say, "How was I being disrespectful, I told you I don' smoke!" And I cut across the street. Well he follows me, and as I glance over my shoulder I see him putting on a pair of *black leather gloves*. I realize shit just got real. So i turn around to stand my ground and **BAM!** Right hook to my chin just as I'm turning around. I stumble back, and am proud to say I barely spilled a drop of my party cup o chai. I regain composure and look up. He's sprinting full speed away from me, into the morning dawn. Never reported because I just had a welt, but damn things can get crazy fast down here.
